{"kind":"request","text":"DX-A2: reads that wait for a head. Child of 2888b81e (Hugh, 28\nOctober).\n\nScope: items 1 to 5 of 2888b81e as written: an optional atLeast (a\nsequence number or a full head) on the summary, items, history and\nentry reads of ScopeApi over HTTP and in process; answer at once when\nthe head is at or past it, otherwise wait up to a bound and answer when\nit arrives, or unavailable with reason behind and the current head when\nthe bound passes; wrong-incarnation for a head of another incarnation;\nthe bound is a member of Bounds; a waiting read holds no storage\ntransaction and does not block the turn; the client handle's reads\naccept a receipt and pass its position; followReceipt uses it instead\nof retrying; reads write nothing; the Readers port decides who may read.\n\nPlanner additions: the compact-card kit's act-then-refresh loop and the\nhosted MCP endpoint's reads use atLeast from the receipt they hold, so\na card shows its own write without polling; name the two call sites in\nthe note. The wait bound is one value for the Worker, set in Bounds,\nbelow the request timeout; a waiting read counts toward the existing\nread limits. J1 (plan 032) rests on this read instead of a retry.\n\nDone when: the witness of item 5 on a real scope, plus one card in the\ntest host that acts and reads its own entry with one request and no\nretry.\n\nSize: small. Order: after J4 (the fork adapter) and the load tasks, and\nbefore the first journey view slice (MVP S2). One gate, exact-head\nreview, PD-2 note.","body":{"conditions":"One gate, exact-head checker review, PD-2 note with the witness.","target_head":"0881c1bca1df31a9fdb4ae72947cbbedf1b3ec51","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}